cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  Si utiliza este software, por favor cítelo como se indica a
  continuación.
title: >-
  Same function, different pruning: the dominant direction of W_O
  under free, soft, and hard intervention
abstract: >-
  Code and measurement scripts for a study of the value-output gauge
  in Vision Transformer attention heads. The dominant direction of a
  head's output projection, v1(W_O), is the cheapest static readout
  available for pruning redundant heads, interpreting their role, or
  routing information between them; this work closes that route
  before it spreads. The direction is not identifiable under the
  value-output gauge: it carries a certified radius of zero, and the
  pruning decision it produces changes under generic
  reparametrization in more than 90% of cases - on a vision-finetuned
  ViT and, by the same closed form and without any training, on a
  pretrained language transformer. In the gauge training leaves, with
  none injected, the factorization moves toward balance - the weight
  reading aligns with the identifiable object to within 18-35 degrees
  - without the two decisions coming to coincide: the most redundant
  pair differs in 37-44% of layers. As an instrument, the
  gauge-invariant response signature v1(C_h^P) measures functional
  diversity without gauge ambiguity, and the coupling between that
  geometry and the function is one-directional across a soft probe and a
  hard variant. Results are established
  on ViT-B/16 (five seeds), contrasted on ViT-L/16 and a frozen
  DINOv2, and extended without training to Pythia-410M.
